<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      The reverse/SWC/day-night broadcasts are sent by the vendor gateway with
      com.szchoiceway.permission.broadcast (CAR_API §1.1). Its protectionLevel is
      almost certainly `signature`, so a normal app cannot be granted it and will
      silently miss those broadcasts. We still declare the <uses-permission> so that,
      once the app is installed as a privileged/system app (pushed to /system/priv-app
      + platform-signed on this rooted device), the receivers start working with no
      code change. As a normal app, CarEvents falls back to the unprotected MCU-level
      reverse events (MCU_MSG_BACKCAR_START/END).
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="com.szchoiceway.permission.broadcast" />

    <!--
      v2.5 ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION: GpsSpeedSource reads road speed from the GPS receiver, which is
      the only numeric speed a normal app can obtain (the gateway broadcasts none — CAR_API
      §1.3). It backs the LAUNCHER_DESIGN §1.4 parked-only gate, so it is declared here beside
      the code that uses it and merged into the app manifest.

      It is a runtime permission: MainActivity asks for it once. On this rooted unit it can also
      be pre-granted with
        `pm grant com.ripostelabs.carlauncher android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`.
      Denied, speed simply stays unknown and the gate fails open by design.

      The head unit has no cell radio, so COARSE alone would not help: only the GNSS chip
      produces a velocity, and it needs FINE.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />

    <!--
      The unit ships a GNSS receiver, but a missing one must not make the APK uninstallable:
      GpsSpeedSource degrades to "speed unknown" on its own.
    -->
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.location.gps" android:required="false" />

</manifest>
